# Scratch test binaries and selftest outputs stay out of the tree.
# Engine objects (build/*.o) and the carbonsim binary remain tracked
# per repo custom (record artifacts, committed with the record).
# s2tui is a live tool, not a record artifact: always untracked.
s2tui
build/test_*
build/verify_cvmds
build/selftest*
# make test writes the suite's output here so the gate can read the
# binary's real exit status instead of a pipeline's (audit fix M5).
build/regression.log

# Auto-generated header-dependency files (-MMD -MP). These are pure
# derived data: a stale one naming a header that no longer exists makes
# make fail hard on a tree that is otherwise fine, and a fresh clone has
# no use for them since every object will rebuild anyway. Tracked engine
# objects are a repo custom about record provenance; dependency graphs
# are not record artifacts.
build/*.d

# Sanitizer scratch output. The record's stderr.txt is tracked; the ASan
# run's is a verification byproduct and is expected to be empty.
stderr_asan.txt
output.asan.txt

# audit/ holds the audit's own working material (audit/README.md). Its build
# products and generated files are derived data: the harnesses are rebuilt by
# audit/run_audit.sh, and 1K4C.cif is the decompressed form of the tracked
# 1K4C.cif.gz.
audit/build/
audit/external/1K4C.cif
audit/scratch/

# ./run writes candidate records here instead of overwriting output.txt
# (audit fix M6). A candidate run is not a record until it is promoted with
# ./run --accept, so keeping the staging area out of the tree is what stops
# an unreviewed run from being committed alongside a record change.
runs/
build/*.log
